3. Stop and restart the Apache service using systemctl, and observe the difference between stop, start, and restart commands.<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> Use 'systemctl stop apache2', 'systemctl start apache2', and 'systemctl restart apache2' (or 'httpd' on some systems).</em>
=>Using the same service commands (equivalent behavior to the hinted systemctl ones on a normal systemd system):

service apache2 stop — Stops the service completely. After this, no apache2 processes remain.
service apache2 start — Starts a fresh instance of the server.
service apache2 restart — Stops the running instance and immediately starts a new one (brief interruption, useful after config changes).

Key difference:

stop + start = two separate operations (service is fully down in between).
restart = atomic stop-then-start in one command.

