5. Write a short comparison (3-4 lines) between Apache and Nginx web servers, mentioning one key use-case for each based on your research.
=>Apache uses a process/thread-based (or configurable MPM) architecture and excels at flexibility, especially with .htaccess per-directory configuration. Nginx uses an event-driven, asynchronous model that handles high concurrency with lower memory use.
Apache key use-case: Shared hosting or traditional LAMP/PHP sites that rely on .htaccess and rich module support.
Nginx key use-case: High-traffic static content, reverse-proxy/load-balancing, or modern containerized/microservices stacks where efficiency under many concurrent connections matters.
